# EVERY SUPPLY WHOSE CAPACITY BUFFER IS SIZED AND WHICH SAYS WHAT IT SERVED, BESIDE THE MOST IT
# COULD HAVE SERVED. One row per examined layer, `violates` where the draw is over the line.
#
# ⭐⭐ THE RULE: a supply cannot serve more than its rating plus the headroom it filed. The
#    nameplate is what it committed, the capacity buffer is how far it can run above that, and
#    the draw is what came out. `draw > nameplate + capacitySlack` is a supply that produced
#    more than it can produce, which is a filing error and never a fact.
#
# ⛔ IT IS THE SUPPLY'S BOUND AND NEVER THE DEMAND'S. "A draw does not exceed what was asked"
#   is the rule this one is NOT, because a shared line's output is partly somebody else's
#   demand -- see layers/drawn.sqlc, where the corpus's one instance is quoted. Bounding the
#   draw by the demand fires on a correct document, which is a rule spending the reader's
#   trust to say nothing.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THREE ANSWERS AND NOT TWO, BORROWED FROM `pm:Fit` RATHER THAN INVENTED HERE. This
#    compared `draw_mode > n_mode + capacity_slack`: two POINTS, in a model whose thesis is
#    that a quantity is a range. `Fit`'s own annotation settles the shape and ends the argument
#    -- "clearance: nameplate.low ≥ demand.high, the WHOLE range clears; transition: the ranges
#    overlap; interference: nameplate.high ≤ demand.low, the WHOLE range interferes. Total and
#    exhaustive ... `mostLikely` DECIDES NOTHING HERE." A rule deciding on the mode was
#    deciding on the one number the schema had already ruled out for this shape of question.
#
# ⛔⛔ SO "DID IT EXCEED" AND "COULD IT HAVE" ARE SEPARATE ANSWERS AND ONLY THE FIRST IS A
#    VIOLATION. The whole draw range above the whole available range is a filing error with no
#    defence. Ranges that OVERLAP are a document that cannot settle its own question, and
#    reporting that as a breach would accuse a filer of something their figures do not say --
#    which is the fault this file already names twice, above and below.
#
# ⚠️ THE MIDDLE ANSWER HAS NO POPULATION TODAY, and that is worth knowing rather than hiding.
#    Of twelve examined rows only three carry a ranged draw or rating at all, and two of those
#    arrived with `support-cover`; all three clear outright. `examples/witnesses/main.rs` is where
#    the other two states are exercised.
#
# ⛔ AN UNMEASURED CAPACITY BUFFER SUSPENDS THE RULE rather than passing it. Six layers do not
#   know how far they can stretch; coalescing that to zero would turn "nobody looked" into
#   "there is no headroom" and manufacture violations out of a gap. A nameplate becomes a
#   ceiling only once somebody says the buffer is empty.
-- pm:Jagged/pm:draw against pm:Nameplate/pm:amount plus pm:Nameplate/pm:capacitySlack.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT d.filing, d.layer,
           -- the WHOLE draw above the WHOLE of what the supply could make
           d.draw_low > d.n_high + d.capacity_high + 1e-9              AS violates,
           CASE WHEN d.draw_low  > d.n_high + d.capacity_high + 1e-9
                THEN format('served [%s, %s] against at most %s: the whole range is over the '
                            'line', d.draw_low, d.draw_high,
                            d.n_high + d.capacity_high)
                WHEN d.draw_high <= d.n_low + d.capacity_low + 1e-9
                THEN format('served [%s, %s] against at least %s: the whole range clears',
                            d.draw_low, d.draw_high, d.n_low + d.capacity_low)
                ELSE format('served [%s, %s] against [%s, %s]: the ranges overlap, so this '
                            'document does not settle whether the supply was overrun',
                            d.draw_low, d.draw_high,
                            d.n_low + d.capacity_low, d.n_high + d.capacity_high)
           END                                                        AS detail
    FROM (
        :compose(layers/drawn.sqlc)
    ) d
    WHERE d.capacity_slack IS NOT NULL
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'draw_exceeds_the_supply'
